    {
      "id": "claim_74286695d8f74a2a9cbaa989886cbb2a",
      "statement": "The harness is parameterised over gatekeepers on purpose (a suite for a new gatekeeper is 'point the harness at the package and plug in a handler module', not a fork), patches checked-in wrangler.jsonc files in memory behind a narrow zod schema so a broken config fails with the field named, and drops the build command when WORKSHOP_INTEGRATION_PREBUILT=1 so isolated test-file processes share one validated build.",
      "evidence": [
