    {
      "id": "claim_1c5fbf817a974967ba3b9ff7e5777296",
      "statement": "The RPC client speaks Cap'n Web over a WebSocket to /api and provides ObserverConfigRecorder, which records the overseer's configure() calls and answers from a scripted queue; the toolkit owns the capnweb boundary — callback stubs are minted with stubFor() from rpc-client rather than an imported RpcStub, because a consumer repo can hold two capnweb copies and a stub from the wrong one fails to serialize (enforced in-repo by a lint rule restricting capnweb value imports to rpc-client.ts).",
      "evidence": [
        {
