    {
      "id": "claim_439fb0a240474fb8bd0c55acea56f1c2",
      "statement": "The fixture makes two deliberate departures for cheapness: no capnweb-validate build step (main points at source) and a single control knob (allow) — a settled denial and an expired credential reach the overseer identically as a thrown error because it deliberately treats every failure as repairable, so the reason string carries the distinction and tests exercise both narratives by choosing reason text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/integration-tests/README.md#L51-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:de9f0ea80714833d869458386f93eb7b493648ebe16f967f0a72c026a3f78de9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3678d2c481764d6bb9ea22c39a9b0184",
      "statement": "Fake timers cannot work in the integration suite: vi.useFakeTimers patches the test process's clock while the code under test reads workerd's clock out of process; they do work for in-isolate unit tests under vitest-pool-workers where the test runs in the same isolate.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L36-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:579b23548aa24e5ff2c8378b28567f928ba8fa58d36dd777aea20577694f121d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b2b1b0c526cf419da22fea80ae87f9ca",
      "statement": "Storage isolation is by convention: server.reset() costs about 3 seconds per call (more than an entire suite run) and restarts the server killing every open WebSocket, so storage persists for the harness's lifetime, no test may assume a clean slate (fresh identities via nextUsernames(), per-test resource URLs, harness-allocated account labels), and the nothing-escaped assertion belongs in afterAll rather than afterEach because with it.concurrent an afterEach fires while siblings are still running.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/integration-testing.md#L66-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:34b9e1ceb524b250a6c62874a515e83c61f521809b4d820642b192bb872aa106:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5c49495680d04c5f9f8c79d356c7e046",
      "statement": "wrangler and workerd versions are coupled: the repo pins workerd through a root overrides entry, a newer wrangler brings a newer miniflare demanding a newer workerd (failing to boot with a compatibility-date error), so the package pins wrangler ~4.104.0 to match and bumping one means bumping the other in step.",
      "evidence": [
